<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Joaquín Balaguer</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1906–2002</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Joaquín <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/balaguer">Balaguer</a> was a Dominican politician and writer who served as president of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dominican-republic">Dominican Republic</a> three times: in 1960–1962, from 1966 to 1978 and from 1986 to 1996. A former aide of the dictator <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rafael-trujillo">Rafael Trujillo</a>, he defeated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/juan-bosch">Juan Bosch</a> in 1966 and ruled for twelve years with repression of the opposition and public building. His later terms were marked by disputed elections.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/joaquin-balaguer.jpg" alt="Joaquín Balaguer" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Joaquin_Balaguer_1977.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
